<style>
    .consent-page {
        max-width: 900px;
        margin: 1em auto;
    }

    .consent-page .panel-body {
        font-size: 1.05em;
        line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .consent-content h2 {
        margin: 0 0 0.35em;
        font-size: 1.35em;
        line-height: 1.3;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .consent-content h3 {
        margin: 1.25em 0 0.45em;
        font-size: 1.15em;
        line-height: 1.3;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .consent-content a {
        color: #0563c1;
        text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .consent-content p {
        margin: 0 0 0.9em;
    }

    .consent-content ul {
        margin: 0 0 0.9em 1.25em;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .consent-content li {
        margin: 0.25em 0;
    }

    .consent-meta {
        margin-bottom: 1em;
    }

    .consent-meta p {
        margin-bottom: 0.35em;
    }

    .consent-actions {
        margin: 28px auto 10px;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .consent-actions .btn {
        margin: 6px;
        white-space: normal;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .consent-actions .btn {
            display: block;
            width: 100%;
            margin: 8px 0;
        }
    }
</style>

<div class="panel panel-info consent-page">
    <div class="panel-heading">
        <h1 class="panel-title" style="font-size:2em">Consent to Participate in a Research Study</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-body">
        <div class="consent-content">
            <h2>The City University of New York</h2>
            <h2>Consent to Participate in a Research Study</h2>

            <div class="consent-meta">
                <p><strong>Title of Research Study:</strong> Student Teacher Judgements about Child Learner Traits</p>
                <p><strong>Principal Investigator:</strong> Anna Workman, M.Phil.<br>Doctoral Candidate, Clinical Psychology<br>Department of Psychology<br>The City College of the City University of New York</p>
                <p><strong>Faculty Advisor:</strong> Sarah O&rsquo;Neill, Ph.D.<br>Associate Professor<br>Department of Psychology<br>The City College of the City University of New York</p>
                <p><strong>Research Sponsor:</strong> Colin Powell Graduate Fellowship</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Overview</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>You are being asked to join a research study. This form gives you important information that will help you decide whether or not to take part. It describes what would happen to you in the study, and helps you understand the reasons why you might or might not want to participate.</li>
                <li>To participate, you must be 18-65 years old, be a current undergraduate or graduate student studying education in the Northeast, able to read and understand English fluently, and have access to a device with a keyboard that is connected to Wi-Fi.</li>
                <li>We cannot tell you every detail of this study ahead of time, but if you are willing to participate under these conditions, we will explain the procedure to you fully after your participation.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Purpose</h3>
            <p>The purpose of this research study is to understand how students studying education make judgments about child learner traits.</p>

            <h3>Procedures</h3>
            <p>If you agree to participate in this research study, we will ask you to do the following:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>You will be asked to complete a couple of questionnaires, which will take approximately 3 minutes.</li>
                <li>You will then be asked to complete a computerized task, which will take approximately 7 minutes, where you will be asked to respond as fast as possible to stimuli that pop up on the screen.</li>
                <li>This study occurs online. You may complete the study at any time you choose, but you will need to use a computer connected to a keyboard. We also highly encourage you to find a quiet and private place to complete the study over a secure Wi-Fi connection.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Time Commitment</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Your participation in this research study consists of completing questionnaires and a computerized task. This will take about 10 minutes to complete.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Potential Risks or Discomforts</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>We will do our best to protect the information we collect from you. However, there remains a risk that someone not involved in the research could access your data. The measures we are taking to reduce the risk are discussed in the <strong><u>Confidentiality</u></strong> section below.</li>
                <li>Some of the questions the researchers ask you may be upsetting, or you may feel uncomfortable answering them. If you do not wish to answer a question, you can skip it and go to the next question.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Confidentiality</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>We will make our best efforts to maintain confidentiality of any information that is collected during this research study. We will protect your confidentiality by securely storing research records, and only researchers will have access to the records. Only those on the research team will know that you are participating and will have access to your records. Steps have been taken to minimize the risk that your privacy will be breached: 1) all study data collected will be identified by a number only; 2) kept separately from identifying information; and 3) kept in confidential password-protected files on a secure device and HIPAA-compliant cloud storage.</li>
                <li>Please be sure to choose a private location for the full duration of the study and complete the tasks over a secure Wi-Fi connection.</li>
                <li>The research team, authorized CUNY staff, and government agencies that oversee this type of research may have access to research data and records in order to monitor the research.</li>
                <li>Publications and/or presentations that result from this study will not identify you by name.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Potential Benefits</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>You will not directly benefit from your participation in this research study.</li>
                <li>The knowledge gained from this study may help us to better understand how future teachers evaluate students&rsquo; behavior.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Costs</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>There will be no cost to you if you participate in this research study.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Payment for Participation</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Eligible participants who complete all study procedures will be entered into a raffle to win a $20 Amazon gift. You will have a one in thirty chance of winning the raffle prize. If you win the raffle prize, you will receive a $20 Amazon gift card via email within one week of winning. The gift card will be emailed to the address you provide. If you do not complete all parts of the study, you will not be entered into the raffle and will not have a chance of being compensated.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>New Information</h3>
            <p>If we learn of anything that may affect your decision to participate, we will inform you as soon as possible. You will then have a chance to reconsider your continuing participation in the research.</p>

            <h3>Participants&rsquo; Rights</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Your participation in this research study is entirely <strong>voluntary</strong>. If you decide not to participate, there will be no penalty to you, and you will not lose any benefits to which you are otherwise entitled.</li>
                <li>You can decide to withdraw your consent and stop participating in the research at any time, without any penalty. You will not be paid for the study activities that you do not participate in after withdrawing.</li>
                <li>You are not giving up any of your legal rights by agreeing to participate.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Questions, Comments or Concerns</h3>
            <p>If you have any questions, comments or concerns about the research, you can talk to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Anna Workman, M.Phil., <a href="mailto:anna.workman93@stu-mail.ccny.cuny.edu">anna.workman93@stu-mail.ccny.cuny.edu</a></li>
                <li>Sarah O&rsquo;Neill, Ph.D., <a href="mailto:soneill2@ccny.cuny.edu">soneill2@ccny.cuny.edu</a></li>
            </ul>
            <p>If you have questions about your rights as a research participant, or you have comments or concerns that you would like to discuss with someone other than the researchers, please call the CUNY Research Compliance Administrator at 646-664-8918 or email <a href="mailto:HRPP@cuny.edu">HRPP@cuny.edu</a>.</p>

            <h3>Agreement to Participate</h3>
            <p>If you agree to participate in this research study, please click on &ldquo;I agree.&rdquo; Please print a copy of this consent form for your records.</p>
            <p>Your agreement indicates that:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>You have read this form.</li>
                <li>You have had your questions answered.</li>
                <li>You voluntarily agree to take part in this research study.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div id="consent-actions" class="consent-actions">
            <button
                pi-message-done
                type="button"
                class="btn btn-primary btn-lg"
                onclick="sessionStorage.setItem('consent_response', 'agree');"
            >
                I agree
            </button>
            <button
                type="button"
                class="btn btn-default btn-lg"
                onclick="sessionStorage.setItem('consent_response', 'no'); var container = document.querySelector('.container'); if (container) { container.style.display = 'none'; } var exitPage = document.getElementById('exit-page'); if (exitPage) { exitPage.hidden = false; } else { document.body.innerHTML = '<main class=&quot;exit-message&quot;><div class=&quot;panel panel-info&quot;><div class=&quot;panel-heading&quot;><h1 class=&quot;panel-title&quot;>Thank You</h1></div><div class=&quot;panel-body&quot;><p>Thank you for your time and interest in this study. You may now close this browser window.</p></div></div></main>'; } document.title = 'Thank You'; return false;"
            >
                I do not wish to proceed with the study
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
